id: new-testament-in-a-year-five-days
title: The New Testament in a year, five days a week
version: 1
creator: Day by Word
summary: The 27 books of the New Testament, Matthew to Revelation, in the
  order they are printed: its 260 chapters, one a reading, five readings a
  week for 52 weeks.
suits: Readers who want a short reading, about three minutes, on five days
  a week, and to read the whole New Testament in a year.
schedule: sequence
behaviors: pace, finish-date
reading-days: 5
coverage: books
canon: protestant
books: MAT, MRK, LUK, JHN, ACT, ROM, 1CO, 2CO, GAL, EPH, PHP, COL, 1TH,
  2TH, 1TI, 2TI, TIT, PHM, HEB, JAS, 1PE, 2PE, 1JN, 2JN, 3JN, JUD, REV
limitations: It reads the New Testament only, in the order it is printed,
  so much that is told in one Gospel is read again in the next. A reading
  is always one chapter, so readings differ in length, from about a minute
  to about nine for the longest chapters.
instructions: Read one chapter on each of your five reading days, in any
  Bible; the other two days of the week are rest days. If you miss a day,
  your next reading waits for you. To finish by a date, choose a finish
  date and Day by Word will show what each reading day asks.
source: An original plan by Day by Word: the New Testament's chapters in
  printed order, one a reading. Reading times are estimated from word
  counts of the World English Bible, a public-domain translation; the plan
  can be read in any translation.
rights: daybyword-original
review: reviewed
